---
import DocsLayout from '@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { DocsTable, Callout } from '@/molecules/DocComponents/DocComponents';

const SIGNALS = [
  ['Manager doctor', 'Configuration, public origin, PostgreSQL, Redis, Coder, secrets, and template source'],
  ['Operation status', 'Queued, running, retryable failure, permanent failure, or success with current step'],
  ['Workspace status', 'Desired and observed state, last heartbeat, Coder build and agent state'],
  ['Nexus logs', 'Issue sync, ticket flow, A2A relay, lifecycle hook delivery, and agent assignment'],
  ['Manager logs', 'Request ID, operation lease, broker exchange, hook ingress, and provisioning errors'],
];
---

<DocsLayout breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Docs', href: '/docs' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/docs/guides' }, { label: 'Operations and Monitoring' }]}>
  <h1>Operations and monitoring</h1>
  <p>Run Manager, Coder, PostgreSQL, Redis, and the secret provider as monitored services. Separate control-plane operation status from tenant agent progress when diagnosing a slow or stuck tenant.</p>
  <DocsTable headers={['Signal', 'What it tells you']} rows={SIGNALS} />
  <h2 id="stuck">Investigate a stuck operation</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Read the Manager operation ID, state, current step, attempt count, and error code.</li>
    <li>Check Manager provisioning logs using the operation and tenant IDs. A queued operation with no attempts points to worker or lease availability; repeated attempts point to a failing step.</li>
    <li>Check Coder build and agent logs if workspace creation has started.</li>
    <li>Use the operation retry control only after identifying and fixing the underlying dependency. Repeated retries do not repair a missing secret, unreachable service, or invalid template.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2 id="health">Monitor the runtime</h2>
  <p>Watch Manager request failures, operation queue age, lease recovery, broker failures, Nexus and worker heartbeats, Redis connectivity, Coder provisioner health, and GitHub rate limits. A running Coder workspace without a Manager runtime heartbeat may still be unusable to OpenFlows.</p>
  <h2 id="changes">Release and recovery</h2>
  <p>Template releases are immutable. Publish a new release name and promote it before rebuilding workspaces. Back up PostgreSQL, Redis, and secret-provider material together. Test restore and credential rotation before production adoption.</p>
  <Callout type="info" title="Operational reference">See the <a href="/docs/architecture/deployment">deployment architecture</a> and the versioned <a href="https://github.com/The-AgenticFlow/OpenFlows/tree/main/docs/implementation/centralized-deployment" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">operator guide</a> for exact commands.</Callout>
</DocsLayout>
